Z||000000||MooCow||03-09-2000||09:55 PM||||Okay I know that there was a thread a while back but it didn't help me out much.  I pay right now for a 91 Ranger v6 about $1200 a year for full coverage and I am 18.  <BR>When I get my Fiero (which I hope will be soon)will my insurance go up or down from this price.  Are Fieros considered a sports car or a commuter car??<BR>                            Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||03-09-2000||10:05 PM||||The insurance guy told me that my Fiero was considered a sports car. But a Corvette, a CRX, and a 260z are also considered a sports car. It really stinks that my 85se with a 4cyl is the same rate as my 88GT. My advice is get liability insurance, get a different car or get married. My liability costs $110 every six months for my Civic. Wife's full coverage is about $300 every six months. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||03-09-2000||10:26 PM||||Just call your insurance co and ask. They will tell you exactly how much.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan||03-09-2000||11:12 PM|||| The four cylinder Fiero was manufactured,marketed,and used as a commuter car.A fellow Fiero owner insured with Allstate told me his rates were high because Allstate considered his four cylinder a sports car.I'm insured with State Farm and my insurance was based on a commuter car for my four cylinder. I expected my rates to go up when I got my 86 SE v6.Much to my amasement, the agent said"same rate". I think normally though the GT is considered a sports car, and higher rates.Hey, don't anyone tell the insurance companies that the SE has the same motor and drivetrain.SE-the most bang for da buck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||03-09-2000||11:25 PM||||My 85 GT (V6), 87 SE (4 banger), and the Batmobile (V8) all cost the same amount through American Family Insurance. Of course, they didn't ask what was in the Batmobile, so I didn't tell them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||chris6878||03-10-2000||01:10 AM||||dont blame ya there...   when i swapped insurace from my 84 coupe to my 85 SE (v6), they didnt ask, i didnt tell  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   they just changed the year and vin # and thats all... when i get a v8 in my 85gt i plan to do the same... (who will ever know)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000006||Oreif||03-10-2000||03:11 AM||||Nationwide Insurance considers The Fiero coupe, the SE and the Formula as commuter cars. They consider the GT a sports car. (I called and asked) The insurance difference between the cars is 12%. According to the agent if it says "GT" it's a sports car. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||03-10-2000||06:11 AM||||Progressive says that a GT and Formula are sports cars so they cost more to insure than the rest.  I just called yesterday about this.  If I put the GT on full coverage and take it off of the Monkeymobile, my premiums will increase by $7/year.  I can live with that.||||reg||1
Z||000008||phillip||03-12-2000||08:05 AM||||i hope this can be considered as the same thread. who has a good multicar rate? i just have liability on three cars with geico and its not bad (74 vette, 84 s-10 blazer,87 fiero, $110 a month ) but it is a major consideration if i add more cars.geico considers all fiero sports cars.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||03-12-2000||11:02 AM||||I use to have Geico but I was able to save more going with Nationwide. With Geico I was paying $135 a month for a 94 Saturn, 98 Durango and my 86 Fiero. Now I pay $89.00 for the same. Note I do have a discount for having my homeowners insurance with them and this is for full coverage on all vehicles.<BR>(married over 35, Fiero as pleasure car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) Geico doesn't do homes and most insurance company's give discounts if you have home and car together. If you shop around you can get decent rates and beat geico's prices. As long as you don't have tickets or accidents.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-12-2000).]||||reg||1
